    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nI found an issue with Visual mode line movement when cmdheight=0 is enabled.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Set:\n\n```lua\nopt.cmdheight = 0 \n```\n\n2. Add mapping:\n\n```lua\nmap({ \"v\", \"x\" }, \"<C-j>\", \":m '>+1<CR>gv=gv\", ns)\nmap({ \"v\", \"x\" }, \"<C-k>\", \":m '<-2<CR>gv=gv\", ns)\n```\n\n3. Enter Visual Line mode (V)\n4. Select more than 2 lines\n5. Press <C-j> or <C-k>\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n\nThe whole selected block should move up/down by one line.\n\nOnly part of the selected block moves, or the movement fails when selecting more than 2 lines.\n\nWorkaround:  \nSetting:\n\n```lua\nvim.opt.cmdheight = 1\n```\n\nfixes the issue.\n\nNeovim version: NVIM v0.12.x\n\nOS: macOS 26.2\n\nI think this may be related to the interaction between cmdheight=0, Ex commands, and Visual selection handling.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.12.4\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nmacOS 26.2\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nalacritty\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-256color\n\n### Installation\n\nhomebrew",
    "closed_at": "2026-07-26T23:32:04Z",
